 "title": "Welcome to Osage County,MO",
 "text": "Welcome to Osage County,MO\nGO\nSearch\nHome\nCounty Offices\n911/Emergency Management\nCircuit Clerk\nCounty Clerk\nCollector of Revenue\nCounty Assessor\nCounty Commission\nCounty Coroner\nCounty Health Department\nCounty Recorder\nCounty Sheriff\nCounty Surveyor\nCounty Treasurer\nProsecuting Attorney\nPublic Administrator\nRoad and Bridge Department\nUniversity of Missouri Extension\nResidents\nChurches\nLibrary\nParks & Recreation\nCounty Schools\nTowns in Osage County\nVoter Registration\nWeather\nCemetery Information\nVisitors\nAccommodations\nDining\nOsage County Historical Society\nUpcoming Events\nVisit Osage County\nCounty Resources\nAmeren Missouri\nLicense DMV\nMissouri Association of Counties (MAC)\nMissouri Court Case\nMissouri Ethics Commission\nMissouri Revised Statutes\nMO Attorney General\nMO Dept. of Natural Resources (DNR)\nMO Secretary of State\nMO State Highway Patrol (MSHP)\nPay Taxes Online\nState Historic Preservation Office (SHPO)\nSunshine Law Request Form\nThree Rivers Electric\nHow Do I\nContact Us\nPay Taxes Online\nCommission Meeting Minutes & Agenda\nView a Map of Osage County\nCounty Recorder\nCounty Recorder\nSub Menu\nRelated\nPages\nCounty Recorder\nRecorder's FAQ's\nHome › County Offices › County Recorder\nThe Recorder of Deeds issues marriage licenses and records real estate transfers, deeds of trust,\npower of attorney, surveys, tax liens and military discharges. The Recorder has records dated back to 1841 to present. Those records include Land transfers and Marriage Licenses. Birth and Death records from 1882 to 1892, are located in the County Clerk’s Office.\nThe public is welcome to do research for family genealogy, marriages, century farms, subdivision plats and restrictions.\nAs of November 1993, all records have been computerized. Which is accessible to the public, banks, title companies and researchers on a public computer in the Recorder’s Office.\nThe office also has Original Marriage Licenses dated 1934 to 1994, which are available to the parties involved in the marriage. Below is a list of fees for recording documents:\nAccepting CASH or CHECK only!\nReal Estate First Page—————————————————$26.00\nFor each additional page thereafter———————————–$ 3.00\n(Page defined as 8 1/2 inches x 11 inches with a 3-inch top margin on the First page)\nPlats First Page ———————————————————-$46.00\nPlats Additional Page Thereafter ————————————-$25.00\n(Page defined as 18 inches x 24 inches)\nSurveys First Page——————————————————$26.00\nEach Additional Page Thereafter ————————————$ 5.00\n(Page defined as 18 inches x 24 inches)\nMarriage License ——————————————————$48.00\n(Missouri no longer has a three day waiting period)\nCertified Marriage License Copy $9.00\nUniform Commercial Code\nUCC – Terminations——————————————————-$6.00\nInfo requests (per debtor name) ————————————$14.00\nCopy request (per debtor name)————————————-$14.00\nCopy charges for recorded documents ——————-$.50 per page\nCertifications—————————————————————-$2.00\nOSAGE COUNTY RECORDER\nCindy Hoffman\n205 E. MAIN STREET\nP.O. BOX 110\nLINN, MO 65051\n(573) 897-2136 – Phone\nrecorder@osagecountymo.gov\nRecorder – Cindy Hoffman – 897-2136\nHours: 8:00 a.m. to 4:30 p.m. Monday to Friday. (Closed major holidays)\nINFO/FORMS:\nRecorder’s FAQ’s\nLINKS:\nMO Recorder’s Association\n© 2017 Osage County,MO\n205 E. Main Street, Linn, MO 65051\nPowered By\nRevize\nLogin\n×\nShare this page\nCopy and past this code into your website.\n<a href=\"http://osagecountygov.com/county_offices/county_recorder/index.php\">Your Link Name</a>\nShare this page on your favorite Social network\nFacebook\nTwitter\nGoogle Plus\nReddit\nClose",
